WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:04.530
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.530 --> 00:08.170
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.170 --> 00:16.100
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.250 --> 00:27.760
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.760 --> 00:33.700
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.700 --> 00:42.640
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.640 --> 00:47.410
Like the wind

00:47.410 --> 00:50.480
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.480 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.520
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.520 --> 01:07.330
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.330 --> 01:13.440
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.440 --> 01:20.180
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.180 --> 01:27.410
The roadless journey continues

01:37.390 --> 01:40.730
Help me... Ellis...

01:40.730 --> 01:44.570
I was... being tricked...

01:44.570 --> 01:48.300
I finally realize that now...

01:48.300 --> 01:50.270
I'll demolish him...

01:50.270 --> 01:53.710
That bastard... With my own hands...

01:53.710 --> 01:55.400
So!

01:57.650 --> 02:02.220
I have to remain myself.

02:02.220 --> 02:05.120
No matter what happens, I...

02:06.790 --> 02:10.260
I see. So it's this thing.

02:10.260 --> 02:12.190
So it was this thing!

02:15.330 --> 02:16.900
Get out...

02:16.900 --> 02:19.870
Get out from inside me...

02:19.870 --> 02:22.130
Rosenberg...

02:29.310 --> 02:31.750
The heart...

02:31.750 --> 02:33.210
...is frail.

02:51.230 --> 02:54.870
Was it... me?

02:54.870 --> 02:58.360
I... did this?

03:01.380 --> 03:04.210
So I did this...

03:04.210 --> 03:07.700
I did this to Nadie...

03:10.250 --> 03:12.720
Yes.

03:12.720 --> 03:14.650
I see...

03:20.500 --> 03:24.300
I'm sorry, Nadie.

03:24.300 --> 03:25.930
I'm sorry.

03:43.380 --> 03:46.250
Was that the right thing to do?

03:46.250 --> 03:48.490
You could have lied to her, too.

03:48.490 --> 03:51.590
You think she would've been satisfied with that?

03:51.590 --> 03:53.960
Ellis isn't stupid.

03:53.960 --> 03:56.300
Besides...

03:56.300 --> 03:58.790
I didn't want to lie.

04:01.400 --> 04:05.710
There once was a group
of people called witches.

04:05.710 --> 04:09.880
As time passed, witches lost their powers

04:09.880 --> 04:13.620
and they became beings of legend.

04:13.620 --> 04:18.320
But science roused the legend from its slumber.

04:18.320 --> 04:21.720
Ellis is a witch made by man's hands.

04:21.720 --> 04:23.930
She's not a child of God.

04:23.930 --> 04:27.290
And she was endowed with powers...

04:28.960 --> 04:31.560
The powers that the people had lost.

04:48.650 --> 04:50.550
Thank you...

05:14.080 --> 05:15.910
It's begun.

05:21.780 --> 05:24.950
Huh? So this is what
ended up happening to me...

05:29.920 --> 05:31.990
Nadie...

05:31.990 --> 05:35.000
Could I... get some water?

05:35.000 --> 05:36.730
Nadie...

05:40.670 --> 05:43.570
She's fine.

05:43.570 --> 05:45.560
It must be out of relief.

06:03.420 --> 06:05.960
You'll have some, right?

06:05.960 --> 06:07.760
Thanks.

06:11.700 --> 06:14.440
What strange turn of events brings you here?

06:14.440 --> 06:16.070
It's by way of thanks.

06:16.070 --> 06:18.370
Because you helped me.

06:20.410 --> 06:22.710
Would you please stop looking at me like that?

06:22.710 --> 06:24.910
I didn't put anything in the cups.

06:30.550 --> 06:32.020
It's bitter.

06:32.020 --> 06:35.720
It needs to be this strong
or you won't feel its effects.

06:35.720 --> 06:37.990
I'm an invalid here.

06:37.990 --> 06:40.130
You're all fine now, aren't you?

06:40.130 --> 06:42.860
Ellis should have patched you up.

06:45.530 --> 06:48.000
A witch... huh?

06:48.000 --> 06:51.410
Yes.

06:51.410 --> 06:52.940
Just as I am.

06:52.940 --> 06:55.540
And here I thought you had
something important to say.

06:55.540 --> 06:59.650
I see. And that's why you
told me that story earlier.

06:59.650 --> 07:02.780
- Yes.
- What's your objective?

07:02.780 --> 07:06.620
Which do you want?
The official one or the private one?

07:06.620 --> 07:10.790
H-Hold on, are you really a witch?

07:10.790 --> 07:13.060
I told you I am, didn't I?

07:16.160 --> 07:18.430
Do you believe me now?

07:18.430 --> 07:20.800
Then, try turning this into iced coffee.

07:20.800 --> 07:22.870
I'll believe you then.

07:22.870 --> 07:24.570
Fine.

07:28.910 --> 07:31.040
Huh? For real?

07:32.980 --> 07:36.180
Um... It's steaming...

07:39.790 --> 07:42.520
I'm a descendant of witches.

07:42.520 --> 07:45.830
But I have no powers.

07:45.830 --> 07:48.700
Powers called magic...

07:48.700 --> 07:52.030
I yearned for it, I researched it,

07:52.030 --> 07:56.540
and I even tried various things...

07:56.540 --> 07:59.240
But all to no avail.

07:59.240 --> 08:01.940
I was left with nothing.

08:01.940 --> 08:07.110
All that I had left was an
overwhelming feeling of desolation.

08:07.110 --> 08:11.150
But my sense of yearning never went away.

08:11.150 --> 08:15.490
Not only did it remain,
but it grew ever stronger...

08:15.490 --> 08:17.120
So that's why...

08:17.120 --> 08:18.960
I wanted to see one...

08:18.960 --> 08:22.130
A real witch.

08:22.130 --> 08:27.160
If I could touch her powers, maybe it
would spark something in me, too...

08:29.040 --> 08:31.710
That's the "private" part.

08:31.710 --> 08:34.080
And the official side of things?

08:34.080 --> 08:37.550
To protect our people.

08:37.550 --> 08:39.580
There was a project

08:39.580 --> 08:45.150
that attempted to artificially recreate
witches for the good of the nation.

08:45.150 --> 08:47.210
You know about it, don't you?

08:59.270 --> 09:02.600
Our people did not look kindly upon it.

09:02.600 --> 09:08.310
Witches were beings who had been
laid to rest by the passage of time.

09:08.310 --> 09:12.210
Their slumber must not be disturbed lightly.

09:12.210 --> 09:17.320
To say nothing of giving life
to witches at the hands of man...

09:17.320 --> 09:20.860
That's why our people set out
to do everything within our means,

09:20.860 --> 09:26.790
and while it took time, we drove
the project into suspension.

09:26.790 --> 09:28.260
But then...

09:31.730 --> 09:33.870
One man...

09:33.870 --> 09:37.700
...relit the candle that was supposed
to have been extinguished.

09:40.310 --> 09:42.080
That man...

09:42.080 --> 09:48.250
Rosenberg. My job is to put
a stop to his sinister design.

09:48.250 --> 09:51.190
Well, I abandoned it part way through, though.

09:51.190 --> 09:52.850
Abandoned it?

09:52.850 --> 09:54.720
I told you, didn't I?

09:54.720 --> 09:57.060
I wanted to see a witch.

09:57.060 --> 10:02.000
So when they suddenly
told me to capture Ellis...

10:02.000 --> 10:06.070
I had no idea something
like that had been ordered.

10:06.070 --> 10:09.070
Considering no one has
shown up to replace me,

10:09.070 --> 10:12.740
they seem to have scrapped that plan, though.

10:12.740 --> 10:15.780
I'm glad I didn't follow those orders.

10:15.780 --> 10:17.650
What was that thing?

10:17.650 --> 10:20.940
That stuff that Ellis was chanting...

10:24.390 --> 10:28.390
A mantle of rainbow-colored
light soars the heavens...

10:28.390 --> 10:33.690
Gallant is the dance of flames
that rend the land asunder...

10:33.690 --> 10:38.000
The roar of the spray in frenzied tumult...

10:38.000 --> 10:41.840
They are all the culmination of deviltry...

10:41.840 --> 10:45.270
Where the crimson essence ultimately leads...

10:47.940 --> 10:51.250
A passage from the legends that have
been passed down among our people.

10:51.250 --> 10:55.980
It celebrates the great powers
that only true witches possess.

10:57.850 --> 11:00.860
True... witches...

11:00.860 --> 11:02.790
The heavens, the earth, and the waters...

11:02.790 --> 11:07.030
Meaning, they're capable of
manipulating all things under the sun?

11:07.030 --> 11:09.260
Yes.

11:09.260 --> 11:10.870
That makes them gods.

11:10.870 --> 11:13.800
Yes, gods.

11:13.800 --> 11:15.800
The power of gods.

11:15.800 --> 11:20.980
And that is the power that Rosenberg seeks.

11:20.980 --> 11:25.410
There's no knowing how
far Rosenberg has read...

11:25.410 --> 11:30.120
But Ellis was definitely
found to have that capacity.

11:30.120 --> 11:32.020
I see...

11:34.790 --> 11:38.290
So that's how it was.

11:38.290 --> 11:40.230
Ellis...

12:00.010 --> 12:01.780
Still the same?

12:01.780 --> 12:04.190
She won't speak to me at all.

12:04.190 --> 12:06.950
It's because of what you said.

12:06.950 --> 12:09.120
She would've found out eventually.

12:09.120 --> 12:12.290
Besides, right now, it's still not too late.

12:12.290 --> 12:17.200
- What?
- I mean that you can still turn back.

12:17.200 --> 12:19.830
I just couldn't figure her out.

12:19.830 --> 12:23.340
She's so pure, or maybe innocent...

12:23.340 --> 12:25.840
That goes for me, too.

12:25.840 --> 12:30.750
And as I worked to keep up with her,
it got so I couldn't just let her be.

12:30.750 --> 12:34.050
It looks like I'm the same.

12:34.050 --> 12:35.850
Blue-eyes...

12:35.850 --> 12:40.960
That's why I want to let her choose for herself.

12:40.960 --> 12:44.020
The path that she thinks she ought to follow...

12:44.020 --> 12:46.960
To be true to your own heart...

12:46.960 --> 12:50.420
That's what's most important, after all.

12:52.530 --> 12:57.170
Goodness gracious. Another hot day.

12:57.170 --> 13:01.140
Was yesterday's storm your doing?

13:01.140 --> 13:04.910
Grandpa, how did you know that?

13:04.910 --> 13:10.250
Of course, I'd know. I know
everything about witches.

13:10.250 --> 13:13.520
I don't want... any of that...

13:13.520 --> 13:19.990
It's a power that only the noble
chosen are permitted to possess.

13:19.990 --> 13:23.130
It's not something that
can be had for the wanting.

13:23.130 --> 13:25.930
- I don't want it.
- Why not?

13:25.930 --> 13:29.000
Because it hurts the people I care about.

13:29.000 --> 13:31.940
That all depends on you.

13:31.940 --> 13:35.140
Power can be good or evil.

13:35.140 --> 13:38.850
You may have been overwhelmed
by the power yesterday,

13:38.850 --> 13:43.150
but in time, you'll surely be able
to impose your will upon it.

13:43.150 --> 13:48.590
And then, it will never hurt someone...

13:48.590 --> 13:51.890
I don't want it.

13:51.890 --> 13:53.360
Ellis...

14:16.050 --> 14:18.520
Ellis.

14:18.520 --> 14:21.550
Where are you going, Ellis?

14:27.230 --> 14:30.600
Bye-bye, Nadie.

14:30.600 --> 14:32.290
Wait!

14:36.470 --> 14:39.210
Nadie, you mustn't go after her.

14:39.210 --> 14:42.310
She... was crying.

14:42.310 --> 14:47.310
Ellis is trying to come up
with an answer on her own.

14:47.310 --> 14:51.120
No... you don't understand anything.

14:51.120 --> 14:53.090
Leave her alone, for her sake.

14:53.090 --> 14:55.590
That's what it means to be free, doesn't it?

14:55.590 --> 14:58.230
That's not being free.

14:58.230 --> 15:00.230
Ellis is lost...

15:00.230 --> 15:02.260
She's suffering...

15:02.260 --> 15:04.670
How can I leave her alone?

15:04.670 --> 15:07.970
That's called being a busybody.

15:07.970 --> 15:10.100
I was free for the longest time.

15:10.100 --> 15:13.210
Because I was all alone.

15:13.210 --> 15:15.640
It's not that I wouldn't depend on anybody.

15:15.640 --> 15:17.510
It's that I couldn't.

15:17.510 --> 15:22.250
Even when I went down the wrong path,
I had no one to tell me otherwise.

15:22.250 --> 15:26.190
You think being free is a wonderful thing.

15:26.190 --> 15:28.460
But you'll find out soon enough.

15:28.460 --> 15:31.530
That being free is actually harder.

15:31.530 --> 15:33.530
More painful.

15:33.530 --> 15:35.430
Nadie...

15:35.430 --> 15:38.600
I wanted someone...

15:38.600 --> 15:40.630
...who would be there for me.

15:40.630 --> 15:42.470
I always have.

15:46.270 --> 15:48.510
She's a good soul.

15:48.510 --> 15:53.110
That's why Ellis opened her heart to Nadie.

15:53.110 --> 15:55.600
Those two shouldn't be apart.

16:21.710 --> 16:23.700
Do you want to go with me?

16:29.580 --> 16:32.620
Ellis...

16:32.620 --> 16:35.190
Do you want to... go with me?

16:35.190 --> 16:37.260
Wiñay Marka?

16:37.260 --> 16:39.050
No.

16:40.190 --> 16:41.630
Let's go...

16:41.630 --> 16:44.720
Somewhere... far away...

16:58.550 --> 17:01.040
Then, let me know if you happen to see her.

17:02.380 --> 17:04.080
Nadie, get in.

17:04.080 --> 17:05.680
I found Ellis!

17:10.660 --> 17:12.360
Does it taste good?

17:12.360 --> 17:18.130
You bought it for me.
Of course it tastes good, Ellis.

17:18.130 --> 17:20.570
Let's get going once we've eaten.

17:20.570 --> 17:23.630
Sure, that's fine with me, Ellis.

17:44.220 --> 17:45.710
L. A?

17:47.190 --> 17:50.200
Blue-eyes?

17:50.200 --> 17:53.400
I was out of line earlier. Sorry.

17:53.400 --> 17:57.140
You're actually a pretty
good person, aren't you?

17:57.140 --> 17:59.540
- I see.
- Huh?

17:59.540 --> 18:04.140
I feel like I sort of understand
what he meant now.

18:04.140 --> 18:06.810
- He?
- Ricardo.

18:06.810 --> 18:10.720
He said something? About me?

18:10.720 --> 18:13.750
It wasn't really anything big.

18:13.750 --> 18:17.160
I picked you for no particular reason,

18:17.160 --> 18:19.560
but I guess I got lucky.

18:19.560 --> 18:22.530
What a thing to say about
the person who betrayed you.

18:22.530 --> 18:25.200
I'm a traitor myself, after all.

18:25.200 --> 18:28.640
Oh, that makes sense now.

18:30.440 --> 18:34.710
What's wrong? L.A., are you okay?

18:34.710 --> 18:36.640
But I broke it...

18:36.640 --> 18:39.580
That bastard...

18:39.580 --> 18:43.320
Rosenberg!

18:43.320 --> 18:44.720
Damn it!

18:44.720 --> 18:47.550
Damn it! I'm me!

18:47.550 --> 18:49.490
Me!

18:51.230 --> 18:54.430
Ah, he's gone...

18:54.430 --> 18:56.630
He's left...

18:56.630 --> 18:58.720
Thank goodness...

19:05.470 --> 19:09.570
It's okay now, Ellis.

19:11.750 --> 19:13.410
Ellis...

19:13.410 --> 19:16.320
Where are you going? Wait...

19:16.320 --> 19:19.290
Together... Ellis...

19:37.170 --> 19:38.800
Ellis.

19:41.680 --> 19:45.780
I'm not letting go, no matter what.

19:45.780 --> 19:47.780
Why?

19:47.780 --> 19:52.450
I don't want to hurt you anymore...

19:52.450 --> 19:55.440
That's why I said bye-bye...

19:58.630 --> 20:02.500
You dummy. You say
something like that again and...

20:02.500 --> 20:04.930
...I'm never forgiving you.

20:08.600 --> 20:11.310
You're so little and yet...

20:11.310 --> 20:13.940
...thinking about such
big things all by yourself...

20:13.940 --> 20:16.540
But...

20:16.540 --> 20:19.580
Try putting yourself in my shoes.

20:19.580 --> 20:21.780
We wanted to get to Wiñay Marka.

20:21.780 --> 20:25.750
That's what we've traveled
all this way for, right?

20:25.750 --> 20:28.760
I have my mind made up, you know.

20:28.760 --> 20:32.390
That I'm going to protect you
with everything I've got.

20:32.390 --> 20:34.460
So you don't have to worry.

20:34.460 --> 20:37.700
I don't care about some witch's powers.

20:37.700 --> 20:39.700
After all, if we go to Wiñay Marka,

20:39.700 --> 20:44.610
we may be able to find the
answers we've been looking for.

20:44.610 --> 20:46.540
It'll be okay.

20:46.540 --> 20:49.780
I'll be by your side, no matter what happens.

20:49.780 --> 20:52.770
I won't let you suffer alone.

20:56.680 --> 20:59.020
Got it, partner?

21:02.560 --> 21:04.350
Yessir.

21:09.530 --> 21:12.330
The heart is frail.

21:12.330 --> 21:13.730
But...

21:13.730 --> 21:18.010
...when two hearts are there for
one another, they are as strong...

21:18.010 --> 21:19.910
...as steel.

21:35.760 --> 21:37.590
Do you feel anything?

21:37.590 --> 21:40.590
I don't feel a thing.

21:40.590 --> 21:42.790
What in the world is this place?

21:56.810 --> 21:59.650
I have been waiting...

21:59.650 --> 22:02.320
...for you two.

22:02.320 --> 22:03.880
You...

22:03.880 --> 22:05.650
Who are you?

22:07.920 --> 22:10.020
I know him.

22:10.020 --> 22:12.660
I...

22:12.660 --> 22:14.090
...know him.

22:14.090 --> 22:18.050
It has been a long time, Ellis.

22:36.550 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.790
Like flowers that never die

22:43.790 --> 22:47.690
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.690 --> 22:55.830
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.040 --> 23:05.650
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.650 --> 23:11.450
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.450 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.530
A night of red stars

23:19.530 --> 23:23.530
The vanishing warmth

23:23.530 --> 23:27.470
I want to keep it here

23:27.470 --> 23:33.870
You, with your eyes closed

23:33.870 --> 23:37.840
Yearning over and over

23:37.840 --> 23:41.180
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.180 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.730
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.730 --> 23:56.720
...everything
